{%- comment -%}
  Outputs 'open' or 'locked'. Driven by customer tags, so access is managed entirely in
  Shopify admin (Klanten > tag toevoegen):
  - D2C mode: always 'open'.
  - B2B mode + "Prijzen alleen voor goedgekeurde klanten": visitors see prices only when
    logged in AND tagged with the configured tag (default: 'zakelijk').
  Leave the tag setting empty to show prices to every logged-in customer.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign access = 'open'
  if settings.store_mode == 'b2b' and settings.b2b_hide_prices
    assign access = 'locked'
    if customer
      if settings.b2b_customer_tag == blank
        assign access = 'open'
      elsif customer.tags contains settings.b2b_customer_tag
        assign access = 'open'
      endif
    endif
  endif
  echo access
-%}
